GitHub #35 (DCS Control, 2026-11-25): DCS no longer crashes at start when a layer below this one faults on a
null-instance xrGetInstanceProcAddr.
- In xrCreateApiLayerInstance the layer reads the extension list it may add to (the D3D11 bridge's XR_KHR_D3D12_enable,
  XR_KHR_visibility_mask) before the next layer has an instance. It asked the next layer's xrGetInstanceProcAddr with
  XR_NULL_HANDLE; Ultraleap's hand tracking layer dereferences that handle, and with Quad Views, frame generation and
  Ultraleap installed DCS Control loaded Ultraleap below OFXR (since the GitHub #20 fix), so DCS crashed at start.
  DCS Control now loads it above OFXR; this patch hardens the layer for any such layer below it.
- instance_extensions_before_create: the loader answers first (resolve_global_function, as for a layer above). An
  application that links the loader statically (DCS: Visualizer.dll exports no loader) or a loader that refuses the
  call while it creates the instance (its global mutex: std::mutex throws on the same thread) leaves the next layer to
  ask, as before, but through guarded_null_instance_lookup / guarded_enumerate_instance_extensions: an access violation
  there is caught and read as "no list", and the instance is created as the application asked. The list is read once
  for both checks.
- tests/layer_call_chain.cpp: null-next-fault (a next layer that faults on XR_NULL_HANDLE, the test's fake loader
  answering: the next layer is never asked, the visibility mask is added) and null-next-fault-noloader (no loader, as in
  DCS: the fault is caught, nothing is added, the instance is created and destroyed). The 0.7.0 layer crashes (access
  violation) on the second.

